    Scaffold the /locate command
    
    Registers /locate structure with a resource-or-tag-key argument, the vanilla
    permission level, and the vanilla translation keys, which already exist in
    pumpkin-data.
    
    Three pure helpers are stubbed with todo!() and a unit test each that defines
    their behaviour: structure name resolution, structure-set membership, and the
    horizontal distance vanilla reports. The executor is left returning not-found
    until those land, because it needs a live World and a generator that may have
    no structure cache, which no unit test can supply.
    
    Structure tags (#minecraft:village) are not supported: pumpkin-data has no
    worldgen/structure tag registry to resolve them against.

